  "note": "The tables of hacks built on pokeemerald-expansion 1.9 to 1.12, such as Emerald Imperium, which keep item, species and ability names in each entry. From 1.13 the item entries hold name pointers. The GF header at 0x100 points at the species (0x1BC), items (0x1C8) and moves (0x1CC), and the RHH header, which Imperium has at 0x1FC, points at the abilities. Imperium is built on 1.10.0, which the RHH header gives at 0x202. Entry sizes follow from the build's options, so a hack built with others has tables of other sizes.",
  "kinds": {
    "item": {
      "length": 80,
      "ranges": [
        {"id": "description", "offset": "0x0C", "length": 4, "type": "u32le", "name": "Description pointer", "confidence": "known", "source": "rom:1d20091c4d936f5eb122db8780554dd0829ffb63"},
        {"id": "name", "offset": "0x14", "length": 20, "type": "text-gen3-intl", "name": "Name", "confidence": "known", "source": "rom:1d20091c4d936f5eb122db8780554dd0829ffb63", "note": "Imperium's items 956 and 957 are all zeros, so they read as blank."},
        {"id": "pocket", "offset": "0x41", "length": 1, "type": "u8", "pockets": {"1": "items", "2": "mega-stones", "3": "balls", "4": "tms", "5": "berries", "6": "key-items"}, "name": "Pocket", "confidence": "known", "source": "rom:1d20091c4d936f5eb122db8780554dd0829ffb63", "note": "Imperium's numbers. It adds a Mega Stones pocket at 2 and moves Key Items to 6, so a hack that keeps pokeemerald-expansion's five pockets reads with the wrong names."}
      ]
    },
    "species": {
      "length": 260,
      "note": "The table's checks read the name's last byte, 0x38, which is its terminator or padding.",
